{"id": "EUVD-2026-76289", "enisaUuid": "cd7ad544-b558-3c59-91c6-c1dce20bd59b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: portman2x4: Check card index validity at probe\n\nAlthough portman2x4 driver has a check of the given devptr->id value,\nit doesn't check for a negative id, which is often given as \"none\" or\nsuch value when bound via sysfs.  This may lead to OOB access for\nindex[] and other parameters.\n\nAdd a sanity check for the card index and warn/correct it if it's a\nvalue out of the range.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:50", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/45ea0707298798678a60ff861b695aea049a5469", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5d7ac5e9ee5ba76b567ace13b46075caf79dcca0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0048994854f3e9c57b7a754de43ef8da5818d140", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64898e9bd8b7b229efa8642b85b56b326a6ec3dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0ce391090809d610647f424b9b1dc24aa2c546fd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d7ef7890e3e35b4ba09e76fc6b72047a1599a5e8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e1ce8ad1009b1736b3044b3324350dcfdd516f42", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3690ef20469d5959378260e2752f2314a2572913"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80966", "GHSA-q972-jx45-qf27"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "032ab907-4e2d-3b3a-b210-53b9c31982dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "757e119bf52b014b3181eed97b01f87a245b8ff9 <45ea0707298798678a60ff861b695aea049a5469"}, {"id": "0452a692-d471-3c2b-a944-5d214a980690", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "0a6567f9-1aaa-32e2-9eb9-cbbe7a052d80", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "757e119bf52b014b3181eed97b01f87a245b8ff9 <0ce391090809d610647f424b9b1dc24aa2c546fd"}, {"id": "0e9c23bc-e87d-3d05-86a0-9407e5ab297b", "p